      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Complement of a Set Without a Venn Diagram",
      "problem": "If $U=\\{2,4,6,8,10,12\\}$ is the universal set and $B=\\{2,6,10\\},$ then the complement of $B$ is",
      "worked_solution": "The complement of $B,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{B},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $B.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $B$ are $4,$ $8,$   and $12.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{B}=\\{4,8,12\\}.\n$$",
